  "body": "document.open()'s method definitions are a bit wrong. It has a single definition, at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dynamic-markup-insertion.html#dom-document-open, even though there are two separate method overloads being defined. In other places in the spec, we use two different `<dfn>`s for two different overloads.\r\n\r\nWe should do the same here, ideally. See https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-context-2d-settransform for the pattern to follow. The work here consists of:\r\n\r\n- Removing the `<dfn>` that opens that section, which I linked to above.\r\n- Changing \"When invoked with two arguments or fewer, the document.open(type, replace) method ...\" and \"When invoked with three arguments, the open(url, name, features) method must run these steps:\" to include `<dfn>`, instead of cross-reference `<span>`s. Their `data-x`s should be so that the first one is `dom-document-open`, and the second one is `dom-document-open-window`.\r\n- Update any references to `dom-document-open` that should now go to `dom-document-open-window`. I think there is probably only one, in the Document IDL block, but it'd be a good idea to check the others.\r\n\r\nI'm marking this as a \"good first issue\", but it's a bit trickier than some others.",
